# Shared DSPy rules (cursor-packs)

When creating or wiring dspy-go modules / interceptors / Create* XML:

- Load skill `dspy-module-patterns`.

When writing or revising module prompts, signatures, or field descriptions:

- Load skill `dspy-prompt-engineering` and its `reference.md` when depth is needed.
- Also load project `pipelines-x-*` prompt overlays if present.

When validation fails, fields look full in logs but parse empty, retries exhaust, or a refinement loop exits early:

- Load skill `dspy-go-debugging`.
- Load skill `dspy-xml-structured-output` for parser details.

When adding a Go gate on model output (lists, ids, verdicts, merge rows), or when tempted to scrape a `*_md` field:

- Load skill `dspy-xml-structured-output` §0 and §0.1 first.
- Discrete contracts MUST be signature fields via strop structured output; `*_md` is counsel only.

When adding or changing a pipeline generator or evaluator, capturing fixtures from module-traces, or adding env-gated live opt-in replay:

- Load skill `dspy-pipeline-isolation`.
- Full JobRunner reseed is the integration check, not the inner loop (golang-quality C17).

Pipeline job layout (JobRunner, per-job clients): load skill `strop-pipeline-pattern` and rule `strop` when orchestration or review is involved. Project overlays (if any) extend — do not replace — the pack pattern.
